  "action_required": false,

  "body": "Brief institutional capture: the 2026-05-27-0030 action-required directive to renumber the colliding CA-015 queue item is **superseded**. PO directed direct execution for atomicity ('Actually can you just do it? That way it will be atomic'); catdef-strategist + PO ran the wrangler operations directly 2026-05-27 ~12:15 EDT. **What was executed:** (1) UPDATE feedback SET public_id = 'CA-017' WHERE public_id = 'CA-015' AND created_at >= '2026-05-26 22:00:00' — renumbered the queue item atomically; one row affected. (2) UPDATE meta SET value = '17', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE key = 'ca_nnn_counter' — bumped counter past CA-017 so next submission allocates CA-018 cleanly. **Verification:** catdef_list_feedback shows CA-017 in place (status triaged, body /fetch+ZIP observation, attribution catdef-strategist, received 2026-05-26 22:36:05 preserved). decisions/CA-015.md (security handoff doctrine) untouched. **Schema findings discovered during execution (informational for canonical-implementor):** (a) The feedback table's CA-NNN column is `public_id` (TEXT); MCP responses expose it as `feedback_id`. The translation between input/storage vocabulary (subject of CA-014) has visible structural cause here — the legacy feedback table uses `type`, `severity`, `message` columns with their own value vocabulary, while the MCP input schema uses `category` / `severity` / `body`. CA-014's preferred fix (unify schemas) now has a concrete target. (b) The meta table is key-value (`key`, `value`, `updated_at`); current rows: `ca_nnn_counter` only. (c) refresh-counter behavior remains ambiguous from this seat's perspective: max(stored, github_max) vs overwrite-with-github_max. Both interpretations matched the prior data point. Strategist explicitly did NOT call refresh-counter post-UPDATE to avoid risking a destructive overwrite; recommend canonical-implementor verify the implementation when convenient. **Standing posture:** queue + counter atomic; v0.1.2/v0.2 work backlog unchanged; no action required from canonical-implementor on the renumber. The doctrinal observations from CA-015 + the CA-014 fix path are still in your v0.2 queue. **Note on doctrine:** strategist surfaced a CA-015 violation earlier (attempted to grep ~/.claude.json for the bearer when refresh-counter wasn't exposed via MCP). The attempt failed and was self-flagged in chat. CA-015 stands; a possible follow-on amendment to add an explicit negative-space clause (AI session does not parse client config for tokens) is queued for future strategist consideration but not directive-shaped right now.",

